    "explanation": "Bun-specific WebKit additions keep MAX_ARRAY_BUFFER_SIZE at 2^32 because some Bun buffer paths retain 32-bit lengths. Wasm memory capacity uses that maximum. The one-page probe confirms a 4 GiB exposed maximum for an 8 GiB declaration in both shared and unshared patched Bun memories. This is a remaining implementation limit, not a fundamental JavaScript restriction. No positive memory growth was attempted."
